  "description": "Certification regarding debarment, suspension, and other responsibility matters for primary covered transactions. The applicant names its organization, the award or project, and its authorized representative; Grants.gov fills in the signature and date.",
  "notes": [
    "The Privacy Act and Paperwork Reduction Act statements, the certification, the civil rights statement and the instructions for certification are quoted exactly as section descriptions. The certification's four statements render as a numbered list, and the civil rights statement links its complaint page and email address, as the DAT asks.",
    "Part B asks an applicant that can't certify to attach an explanation. The form has no attachment field for it, like the paper form; the explanation goes with the application.",
    "Signature and Submitted Date are filled in by the API on submission (`gg_post_population` rules `signature` and `current_date`), so the form shows them read-only.",
    "Labels are the DAT's, in title case. Standardizing them on the question bank's labels comes later."
  ],
